---
const tickers = [
  { sym: "SPX", chg: "+0.42%" },
  { sym: "NDX", chg: "+0.61%" },
  { sym: "DJI", chg: "-0.08%" },
  { sym: "RUT", chg: "+1.12%" },
  { sym: "VIX", chg: "-2.41%" },
  { sym: "GLD", chg: "+0.18%" },
  { sym: "USO", chg: "-0.74%" },
  { sym: "BTC", chg: "+3.05%" },
  { sym: "TSLA", chg: "+1.84%" },
  { sym: "NVDA", chg: "+2.21%" },
  { sym: "AAPL", chg: "-0.34%" },
  { sym: "MSFT", chg: "+0.55%" },
];
---

<!-- Hairline ticker strip just under the topbar — purely decorative -->
<aside class="border-border/60 bg-card/40 relative overflow-hidden border-b" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="ticker num text-muted-foreground py-2 text-[0.6875rem] tracking-tight">
    {
      [...tickers, ...tickers].map((t) => (
        <span class="mx-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-foreground font-medium">{t.sym}</span>
          <span class:list={[t.chg.startsWith("-") ? "text-destructive" : "text-positive"]}>{t.chg}</span>
        </span>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</aside>

<main class="relative">
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden">
    <div class="bg-grid pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 opacity-60" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div
      class="relative mx-auto grid w-full max-w-6xl gap-12 px-6 pt-20 pb-24 sm:px-10 sm:pt-28 sm:pb-32 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-8"
    >
      <!-- Left column: editorial copy block -->
      <div class="reveal lg:col-span-8" style="animation-delay: 80ms">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="bg-foreground inline-block h-px w-8" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          Issue №01 · Research, on demand
        </p>

        <h1 class="display text-foreground text-[clamp(2.75rem,7.5vw,5.75rem)]">
          Quiet conviction,<br />
          <span class="font-light italic">measured</span> in markets.
        </h1>

        <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-8 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed sm:text-xl">
          Quant is an AI research desk for individual investors. Compose a thesis, pick a model, and receive long-form,
          citation-backed analysis on any sector, ticker, or macro event — written, saved, and continuable.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <a
            href="/auth/signup"
            class="bg-foreground text-background group inline-flex items-center gap-3 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium tracking-tight transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
          >
            <span
              class="bg-primary text-primary-foreground -ml-2 inline-flex h-5 w-5 items-center justify-center text-[0.625rem]"
              >→</span
            >
            Open a research account
          </a>
          <a
            href="/auth/signin"
            class="text-foreground border-foreground/30 hover:border-foreground inline-flex items-center px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium tracking-tight transition-colors"
            style="border-top: 1px solid; border-bottom: 1px solid;"
          >
            Sign in
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right column: vertical metadata strip -->
      <aside class="reveal lg:col-span-4 lg:pt-6 lg:pl-8" style="animation-delay: 180ms">
        <dl class="border-border/70 grid grid-cols-2 gap-y-6 border-l pl-6 text-sm lg:grid-cols-1">
          <div>
            <dt class="eyebrow mb-1.5">Coverage</dt>
            <dd class="font-display text-2xl leading-none">Sectors · Indices · Tickers</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="eyebrow mb-1.5">Models</dt>
            <dd class="num text-base">GPT-4o · Claude 3.5 · GPT-4o-mini</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="eyebrow mb-1.5">Citations</dt>
            <dd class="text-base">Web-search grounded, source-listed.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="eyebrow mb-1.5">Posture</dt>
            <dd class="text-base italic">Informational only. Not advice.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THREE-CARD MANIFESTO -->
  <section class="border-border/60 bg-card/40 border-y">
    <div class="mx-auto grid w-full max-w-6xl grid-cols-1 divide-y px-0 sm:grid-cols-3 sm:divide-x sm:divide-y-0">
      {
        [
          {
            n: "01",
            head: "Compose a thesis",
            body: "Stash reusable prompts — sector overview, valuation check, news catalyst — and dispatch them against any subject without retyping the scaffolding.",
          },
          {
            n: "02",
            head: "Stream the answer",
            body: "Output renders token-by-token as the model thinks. Continue, branch, or quote any prior run — your work tree is saved as you go.",
          },
          {
            n: "03",
            head: "Own the chain",
            body: "Bring your own keys (OpenAI, Anthropic). No model lock-in, no opaque pricing. The research desk is yours; we just laid out the desk.",
          },
        ].map((item, i) => (
          <div class="reveal divide-border/60 group px-8 py-10 sm:py-14" style={`animation-delay: ${260 + i * 90}ms`}>
            <span class="num text-muted-foreground text-xs">{item.n} ──</span>
            <h3 class="font-display mt-4 text-2xl leading-tight tracking-tight">{item.head}</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">{item.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- "ANATOMY OF A RUN" — annotated sample -->
  <section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 sm:px-10 sm:py-28">
    <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-12">
      <header class="lg:col-span-4">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-4">Anatomy of a run</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-4xl leading-[1.05] tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
          One prompt.<br />
          <span class="font-light italic">One thesis.</span><br />
          A paper trail.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-6 max-w-sm text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Every analysis is saved with its prompt snapshot, model, citations, and lineage — so you can revisit it
          tomorrow and know exactly what you asked, who answered, and what they read.
        </p>
      </header>

      <article
        class="border-border/70 bg-card relative border lg:col-span-8"
        style="box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 0 color-mix(in oklch, var(--foreground) 8%, transparent);"
      >
        <header class="border-border/70 flex items-center justify-between border-b px-6 py-3 text-xs">
          <span class="num text-muted-foreground">RUN-00482 · openai/gpt-4o · 2026-06-05 09:14</span>
          <span class="text-positive flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span class="bg-positive inline-block h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full"></span>
            saved
          </span>
        </header>
        <div class="space-y-5 px-6 py-6">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow mb-1.5">Topic</p>
            <p class="text-base font-medium">Renewable energy sector — H2 2026 outlook</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow mb-1.5">Prompt</p>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground border-foreground/30 border-l-2 pl-3 text-sm italic">
              Survey the sector. Macro tailwinds. Three names to watch. Material risks. Cite primary sources.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Output (excerpt)</p>
            <div class="text-foreground/85 space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              <p>
                <strong class="text-foreground">Macro.</strong> IRA tailwinds remain intact through 2026; pace of interconnect
                queue clearance is the swing variable. Storage attachment rates continue to compress LCOE...
              </p>
              <p>
                <strong class="text-foreground">Names.</strong>
                <span class="num"> NEE</span>, <span class="num">FSLR</span>, <span class="num">ENPH</span> — each on a distinct
                thesis (utility-scale, modules, residential). Detail in §3...
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="border-border/70 flex items-center justify-between border-t pt-4 text-xs">
            <span class="num text-muted-foreground">7 sources · 1,842 tokens</span>
            <span class="text-foreground inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-medium"> Continue analysis → </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- DISCLAIMER STRIP -->
  <section class="border-border/60 border-t">
    <div
      class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-col gap-4 px-6 py-10 text-xs sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between sm:px-10"
    >
      <p class="eyebrow">Important · Read</p>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        Quant generates AI-assisted research. Output may be incomplete or wrong; verify everything against primary
        sources before making any investment decision. Past performance ≠ future returns. You are the analyst of record.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
